WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.439 --> 00:00:01.964
- Dreams do come true!

00:00:01.964 --> 00:00:03.945
I've chased one for last 21 years.

00:00:03.945 --> 00:00:06.897
When I walk and do bad,
I should know that yes,

00:00:06.897 --> 00:00:09.297
I've prepared to the best of my ability.

00:00:09.297 --> 00:00:10.980
I couldn't have done anything better.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:11.950
My father told me that

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:14.320
"Don't, don't look to find shortcuts."

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:17.581
"There are going to be tough
phases in your career."

00:00:17.581 --> 00:00:20.151
- He's a former Indian
cricketer and captain.

00:00:20.151 --> 00:00:21.840
He's the only player to have scored

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.307
100 international centuries.

00:00:24.307 --> 00:00:25.474
He's widely regarded as one

00:00:25.474 --> 00:00:27.523
of the greatest batsmen of all time.

00:00:27.523 --> 00:00:28.818
He's Sachin Tendulkar.

00:00:28.818 --> 00:00:31.556
And here's my take on his
top 10 rules for success.

00:00:31.556 --> 00:00:33.151
Rule number one is my personal favorite.

00:00:33.151 --> 00:00:34.960
And make sure to stick
around all the way to the end

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:36.744
for some special bonus clips.

00:00:36.744 --> 00:00:37.969
And as always if he says something

00:00:37.969 --> 00:00:39.839
that really, really resonates with you,

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:41.405
please leave it down in the comments below

00:00:41.405 --> 00:00:43.055
and put quotes around it so other people

00:00:43.055 --> 00:00:44.854
can be inspired as well.

00:00:44.854 --> 00:00:47.738
(whooshing noise)

00:00:47.738 --> 00:00:51.155
(uplifting string music)

00:00:57.933 --> 00:01:00.940
- Something which is
really, really important is,

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:04.812
which I believed, you
have to chase your dreams.

00:01:04.812 --> 00:01:06.398
Dreams do come true!

00:01:06.398 --> 00:01:08.823
I've chased one for last 21 years.

00:01:08.823 --> 00:01:12.156
One World Cup for India, after 21 years.

00:01:13.132 --> 00:01:15.023
So dreams do come true.

00:01:15.023 --> 00:01:19.190
It may take a bit longer than
some, but they do come true.

00:01:20.551 --> 00:01:24.772
Sometimes what happens,
that, we push ourselves,

00:01:24.772 --> 00:01:28.318
but not enough, because
we try and then we say,

00:01:28.318 --> 00:01:29.740
we find excuses, we say that

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:32.905
"Oh enough, I've tried,
it's not happening."

00:01:32.905 --> 00:01:34.211
And you give up.

00:01:34.211 --> 00:01:37.632
And one extra step,
success is waiting for you.

00:01:37.632 --> 00:01:40.816
Which you sometimes don't end up taking.

00:01:40.816 --> 00:01:43.376
So always be prepared to push yourself.

00:01:43.376 --> 00:01:47.543
Fearless and, the other way
to describe that is confident.

00:01:48.393 --> 00:01:49.872
You know, self belief.

00:01:49.872 --> 00:01:52.835
I believe that if you're
confident of your ability,

00:01:52.835 --> 00:01:56.626
if you're confident of your
preparations, you know.

00:01:56.626 --> 00:01:57.886
Some people call it fearless,

00:01:57.886 --> 00:01:59.540
some people call it confidence.

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:03.035
And I feel I'm confident of what I do.

00:02:03.035 --> 00:02:05.168
I fail sometimes, I succeed sometimes.

00:02:05.168 --> 00:02:06.654
So that's fair enough.

00:02:06.654 --> 00:02:09.847
It's a package deal it
comes with that package.

00:02:09.847 --> 00:02:13.817
Failures and success, so I
would put it differently.

00:02:13.817 --> 00:02:16.720
I'm confident and I trust my instincts.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:21.381
When I first played for
India, which was my dream,

00:02:21.381 --> 00:02:25.415
my father took me aside and told me that,

00:02:25.415 --> 00:02:29.415
"You have reached your
landmark, now what next?"

00:02:30.548 --> 00:02:34.243
So I told him that "I'm going
to continue playing for India."

00:02:34.243 --> 00:02:35.543
So he said,

00:02:35.543 --> 00:02:39.710
"You know everything in life
is going to be temporary,

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:43.974
"you'll play cricket
for 10, 15 years, maybe,

00:02:43.974 --> 00:02:48.200
"maybe 20 years, but what
happens beyond that?"

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:51.422
"Because everything is going
to be temporary in your life."

00:02:51.422 --> 00:02:56.136
"The only thing which will
stay permanently with you

00:02:56.136 --> 00:02:59.954
"till your last breath is
the person that you are."

00:02:59.954 --> 00:03:02.915
"The nature of a person has to be good."

00:03:02.915 --> 00:03:06.332
(crowd cheers and claps)

00:03:07.872 --> 00:03:10.856
So he said, "Lot of things will happen

00:03:10.856 --> 00:03:13.771
"when you play cricket,
people will appreciate."

00:03:13.771 --> 00:03:18.560
"But I would be happier if
people appreciated you more

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:21.433
"as a good person, so try
and be a good person."

00:03:21.433 --> 00:03:24.600
And something I would want all of you,

00:03:25.815 --> 00:03:30.809
boys and girls to follow, try
and be a good person first.

00:03:30.809 --> 00:03:32.451
I think...

00:03:32.451 --> 00:03:36.034
to respect your
opposition, your teammates,

00:03:37.409 --> 00:03:39.076
is really important.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:43.144
I can understand everyone
is out there to win.

00:03:43.144 --> 00:03:45.809
Not everyone can be winners,

00:03:45.809 --> 00:03:49.145
but you can definitely
win everyone's hearts.

00:03:49.145 --> 00:03:49.978
You can...

00:03:51.167 --> 00:03:55.536
You can win some games,
you can lose some games.

00:03:55.536 --> 00:03:58.953
In my career I haven't won all the games,

00:04:00.947 --> 00:04:04.349
but something which sport teaches you,

00:04:04.349 --> 00:04:08.901
is when there is failure, when
you're faced with challenges,

00:04:08.901 --> 00:04:12.239
sport teaches you to get
back on your feet again

00:04:12.239 --> 00:04:15.384
and compete harder in the right spirit.

00:04:15.384 --> 00:04:18.271
And that's what my
message to you would be,

00:04:18.271 --> 00:04:21.624
compete hard, but play
in the right spirit,

00:04:21.624 --> 00:04:23.785
and respect your sport above all.

00:04:23.785 --> 00:04:27.018
To me, re-match preparation
is extremely important.

00:04:27.018 --> 00:04:30.351
Because, that's something
which is within my control.

00:04:30.351 --> 00:04:33.369
When I walk and do bad,
I should know that yes,

00:04:33.369 --> 00:04:35.770
I've prepared to the best of my ability.

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:37.735
I couldn't have done anything better.

00:04:37.735 --> 00:04:42.193
That is when I feel that I'm
ready to go out and play.

00:04:42.193 --> 00:04:44.904
There is no player in the
world who can actually walk out

00:04:44.904 --> 00:04:47.320
and say, "Today I'm going to score 100."

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:50.146
Or, "I will get minimum
5 kicks and come back."

00:04:50.146 --> 00:04:52.499
Sometimes it happens,
sometimes it doesn't happen.

00:04:52.499 --> 00:04:55.985
But I believe in controlling
the controllables.

00:04:55.985 --> 00:05:00.615
Something where we don't have
control on certain things.

00:05:00.615 --> 00:05:03.692
Those things you obviously
cannot waste your energy

00:05:03.692 --> 00:05:06.132
in trying to figure out
"How can I control this?"

00:05:06.132 --> 00:05:08.582
You would much rather
focus all your energy

00:05:08.582 --> 00:05:11.316
on the things that you can control.

00:05:11.316 --> 00:05:14.091
Get the best results possible.

00:05:14.091 --> 00:05:17.584
But, making an effort is in your hands.

00:05:17.584 --> 00:05:20.475
Giving 100% is in your hands.

00:05:20.475 --> 00:05:23.469
Sometimes you end up with good
results, sometimes you don't.

00:05:23.469 --> 00:05:25.769
Trying, giving 100% is in your hands.

00:05:25.769 --> 00:05:27.170
That is what matters to me.

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:31.707
You all have dreams, you
all have vision and life.

00:05:31.707 --> 00:05:34.338
Of what you want to be.

00:05:34.338 --> 00:05:37.803
To become a priceless, precious diamond.

00:05:37.803 --> 00:05:42.129
You all are talented, you
all are sent down by God

00:05:42.129 --> 00:05:44.010
with some of the other talent.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.738
We just need to identify that.

00:05:46.738 --> 00:05:50.488
And then from an uncut, unpolished diamond

00:05:50.488 --> 00:05:53.268
to become a polished, priceless diamond,

00:05:53.268 --> 00:05:54.389
it is a process,

00:05:54.389 --> 00:05:58.528
it's a journey where
the path won't be easy.

00:05:58.528 --> 00:06:01.759
Sometimes when you're
trying to do certain things,

00:06:01.759 --> 00:06:04.377
there might be obstacles.

00:06:04.377 --> 00:06:07.377
Don't give up, don't find shortcuts.

00:06:09.291 --> 00:06:13.458
I think it is important to
follow the right path always.

00:06:15.825 --> 00:06:19.065
And in tough times, tough men last.

00:06:19.065 --> 00:06:22.097
So I'm very, very confident
that if you follow

00:06:22.097 --> 00:06:23.809
the right things in life,

00:06:23.809 --> 00:06:26.241
you will be able to achieve your dreams.

00:06:26.241 --> 00:06:29.658
To me, cricket taught me a lot of things.

00:06:31.179 --> 00:06:34.096
Right from my school days, cricket,

00:06:35.203 --> 00:06:38.036
taught me to prepare for an event.

00:06:39.368 --> 00:06:43.105
To plan how I want to move forward.

00:06:43.105 --> 00:06:46.113
And then to be able to execute those plans

00:06:46.113 --> 00:06:48.046
was even more important.

00:06:48.046 --> 00:06:51.721
My father was a writer, he was a poet.

00:06:51.721 --> 00:06:54.023
He said, "Whatever you want to be in life,

00:06:54.023 --> 00:06:56.696
"I don't expect you to become a poet,

00:06:56.696 --> 00:07:00.166
"your passion is cricket,
so in cricket you make sure

00:07:00.166 --> 00:07:01.702
"that you give your best."

00:07:01.702 --> 00:07:03.892
(uplifting music)

00:07:03.892 --> 00:07:04.844
My father told me that

00:07:04.844 --> 00:07:07.213
"Don't, don't look to find shortcuts."

00:07:07.213 --> 00:07:10.661
"There are going to be
tough phases in your career,

00:07:10.661 --> 00:07:14.439
"it doesn't matter if you fail
following the right path."

00:07:14.439 --> 00:07:16.355
"So, keep following the right path."

00:07:16.355 --> 00:07:20.889
"As long as you know you,
your heart tells you that yes,

00:07:20.889 --> 00:07:23.453
"today you've tried your best."

00:07:23.453 --> 00:07:26.294
"That is what I expect from
you, nothing more than that."

00:07:26.294 --> 00:07:30.264
Any team sport, there are
certain teams targets.

00:07:30.264 --> 00:07:35.071
And those targets should
always be in the forefront.

00:07:35.071 --> 00:07:38.490
And then you'll always find
in a team sport on a given day

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:39.985
they'll be certain individuals

00:07:39.985 --> 00:07:42.586
who would perform better
than the other ones.

00:07:42.586 --> 00:07:43.935
You just need to understand that

00:07:43.935 --> 00:07:46.953
the guys who are in great form,

00:07:46.953 --> 00:07:49.484
the others have to play
around them and chip in.

00:07:49.484 --> 00:07:52.915
In any, whichever manner possible.

00:07:52.915 --> 00:07:55.248
And I feel great individuals

00:07:56.269 --> 00:07:59.328
and great performances build a team.

00:07:59.328 --> 00:08:02.191
Which produces brilliant performances.

00:08:02.191 --> 00:08:04.850
You need solid individuals
who come together

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:08.988
and play as a team and
then achieve the results,

00:08:08.988 --> 00:08:11.654
which we all aspire to.

00:08:11.654 --> 00:08:15.613
It is fantastic to be part
of Indian cricket team,

00:08:15.613 --> 00:08:17.476
last so many years that I've been part of.

00:08:17.476 --> 00:08:18.955
I've thoroughly enjoyed.

00:08:18.955 --> 00:08:20.587
There have been ups and downs,

00:08:20.587 --> 00:08:23.286
but it has taught us a lot in life.

00:08:23.286 --> 00:08:25.394
Going with the team
through those ups and downs

00:08:25.394 --> 00:08:27.379
is a terrific journey.

00:08:27.379 --> 00:08:29.811
I have thoroughly
enjoyed being part of it.

00:08:29.811 --> 00:08:32.005
No just to clarify to everyone,

00:08:32.005 --> 00:08:34.275
that I don't play for milestones.

00:08:34.275 --> 00:08:36.789
(uplifting string music)

00:08:36.789 --> 00:08:38.206
I play for India.

00:08:40.091 --> 00:08:42.726
The dream was to play for India.

00:08:42.726 --> 00:08:46.393
(powerful orchestral music)

00:09:00.110 --> 00:09:03.777
(powerful orchestral music)

00:09:11.926 --> 00:09:12.759
(crowd cheering)

00:09:12.759 --> 00:09:14.426
Thank you very much.

00:09:15.915 --> 00:09:18.929
If I missed out on saying something,

00:09:18.929 --> 00:09:22.047
missed out on a few names
I hope you understand.

00:09:22.047 --> 00:09:22.880
Goodbye.

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:23.829
(crowd cheering)

00:09:23.829 --> 00:09:27.246
- [Crowd] Sachin, Sachin, Sachin, Sachin.

00:09:30.482 --> 00:09:33.065
Sachin, Sachin, Sachin, Sachin.

00:09:36.757 --> 00:09:38.007
Sachin, Sachin.

00:09:39.994 --> 00:09:41.911
Sachin, Sachin, Sachin.

00:09:47.191 --> 00:09:48.687
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:09:48.687 --> 00:09:51.104
I made this video because
Binay asked me to,

00:09:51.104 --> 00:09:52.190
so if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:53.896
that you want me to profile next,

00:09:53.896 --> 00:09:55.319
leave it down in the comments below

00:09:55.319 --> 00:09:56.456
and I'll see what I can do.

00:09:56.456 --> 00:09:57.289
I'd also love to know which

00:09:57.289 --> 00:09:59.409
of the top 10 rules meant the most to you,

00:09:59.409 --> 00:10:01.834
had the biggest impact, what
did you really take from this.

00:10:01.834 --> 00:10:03.216
I'd love to hear from you.

00:10:03.216 --> 00:10:04.448
Please leave it in the comments,

00:10:04.448 --> 00:10:06.200
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:07.768
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:10:07.768 --> 00:10:09.196
I believe in you,

00:10:09.196 --> 00:10:11.646
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:10:11.646 --> 00:10:14.119
and whatever your one word is.

00:10:14.119 --> 00:10:16.470
Much love, I'll see you soon.

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:19.303
(whooshing noise)

00:10:22.518 --> 00:10:24.962
- I always wanted to win the world cup.

00:10:24.962 --> 00:10:26.832
That was the reason I started.

00:10:26.832 --> 00:10:30.999
And as the time went by I
started enjoying cricket,

00:10:32.213 --> 00:10:35.638
and I started realizing
the challenges of cricket.

00:10:35.638 --> 00:10:39.627
And my coach was instrumental
and along with my brother.

00:10:39.627 --> 00:10:40.460
- [Interviewer] Had you--

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:44.293
- To my elder brother
Ajit, to make me realize

00:10:45.377 --> 00:10:49.127
the importance of leading
a disciplined life,

00:10:50.892 --> 00:10:52.825
a focused life.

00:10:52.825 --> 00:10:53.658
And to,

00:10:56.938 --> 00:10:59.644
to make me push harder,

00:10:59.644 --> 00:11:03.811
they found reasons and even
towards the end of my career,

00:11:05.751 --> 00:11:08.056
I followed that formula.

00:11:08.056 --> 00:11:12.274
If I scored once, let the rest
of the world talk about it.

00:11:12.274 --> 00:11:14.202
I think about the next game.

00:11:14.202 --> 00:11:17.367
And that, right from my school days became

00:11:17.367 --> 00:11:21.226
an unwritten formula, an
unwritten law at home.

00:11:21.226 --> 00:11:23.763
That we don't talk about last game,

00:11:23.763 --> 00:11:25.854
we talk about next game.

00:11:25.854 --> 00:11:29.186
And however many runs I score,

00:11:29.186 --> 00:11:32.681
I wanted to go out and
score more than that.

00:11:32.681 --> 00:11:36.557
So, if I didn't score, I
would have a restless night.

00:11:36.557 --> 00:11:39.711
If I scored runs, I would
still have a restless night.

00:11:39.711 --> 00:11:42.142
Thinking that, how am
I going to score more?

00:11:42.142 --> 00:11:44.512
And that's how it all happened, I mean I,

00:11:44.512 --> 00:11:46.429
I normally don't discuss numbers

00:11:46.429 --> 00:11:50.730
but this is something that I
must share with all of you.

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:54.397
Towards the end of my
school cricket career,

00:11:55.332 --> 00:11:59.503
I already started playing
first-class cricket.

00:11:59.503 --> 00:12:01.233
And the last season I can proudly say that

00:12:01.233 --> 00:12:03.483
I averaged thousand and 25,

00:12:04.581 --> 00:12:06.639
because I only got out
once in the whole season.

00:12:06.639 --> 00:12:07.586
(crowd and interviewer laugh)

00:12:07.586 --> 00:12:08.836
- [Sachin] And.

00:12:10.914 --> 00:12:11.747
My...

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:17.180
My brother and my coach
was instrumental in that

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:19.930
because every time I scored runs,

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:24.378
none of them said "Well
played" to me and that's why

00:12:24.378 --> 00:12:28.691
in my farewell speech, I said to my coach,

00:12:28.691 --> 00:12:32.015
"At least now you can take a
chance by saying well done."

00:12:32.015 --> 00:12:32.956
(interviewer and crowd laughs)

00:12:32.956 --> 00:12:35.436
- There are no more matches in my career.

00:12:35.436 --> 00:12:38.423
But, something that I lived for

00:12:38.423 --> 00:12:42.516
was appreciation from
my coach and my brother.

00:12:42.516 --> 00:12:44.374
Which never happened.

00:12:44.374 --> 00:12:47.612
And that was something
which, you know sort of

00:12:47.612 --> 00:12:50.612
kept me giving my best all the time.

00:12:51.485 --> 00:12:52.843
Every individual it is important

00:12:52.843 --> 00:12:57.010
to have some kind of exercise
and lead a healthy life.

00:12:58.443 --> 00:13:02.227
For me I feel, you know,
just the basic training

00:13:02.227 --> 00:13:05.083
just to keep in good shape
and then during the season

00:13:05.083 --> 00:13:08.261
and off-season we have different plans.

00:13:08.261 --> 00:13:12.562
And sometimes it is about
improving your fitness.

00:13:12.562 --> 00:13:15.883
And sometimes it is about
just maintaining that level.

00:13:15.883 --> 00:13:19.221
So it depends what phase
you're going through,

00:13:19.221 --> 00:13:20.468
during the season.

00:13:20.468 --> 00:13:23.516
Obviously it is difficult
to push hard all the time

00:13:23.516 --> 00:13:24.988
because you're playing matches.

00:13:24.988 --> 00:13:28.300
But, just preseason is the period where

00:13:28.300 --> 00:13:31.898
one would want to try harder
and improve the fitness level.

00:13:31.898 --> 00:13:35.074
But generally, in between
the matches it is to

00:13:35.074 --> 00:13:37.501
do with just maintenance and recovery.

00:13:37.501 --> 00:13:40.384
You need a good recovery
session so that you're fresh

00:13:40.384 --> 00:13:41.709
for the next game.

00:13:41.709 --> 00:13:45.396
Then go out there and perform
equally or even better.

